    "tree_id": "1e635388cf34c1343fdc80df5c7c56d955ea4eee",
    "message": "fix(chunker): hard-split oversized cur in the else branch — 630 silently-truncated chunks -> 384 documented\n\nFull-corpus replay (312,506 rows, pinned e5 tokenizer) proved the\nelse-branch of chunk_definition flushed an oversized cur as-is when a\n>1049-char sentence arrived while cur was non-empty: 310 rows produced\noversized chunks (max 13,130 chars) and 630 of 350,829 chunks (0.180%)\nexceeded the e5 max_seq_length of 512 tokens and were SILENTLY truncated\nby sentence-transformers (vector covers only the first ~510 tokens; no\nexception is raised). Worst vector covered ~13% of its chunk text.\n\nFix mirrors branch-1's hard-split loop in the else branch, so every\nemitted chunk is <= chunk_chars. Regression tests added (they fail on\nthe old code: [12, 1772] chunk lens).\n\nResidual after the fix: 384 of 351,156 chunks (0.109%) still exceed 512\ntokens — all <=1200 chars, worst 845 tokens; caused by vocalized Arabic\nharakat (separate XLM-R tokens, 0.71 chars/token) which the char-based\nchunk contract cannot bound. Documented as pins.json\nprebuilt_index.known_truncations; BM25 sparse + payload always cover the\nfull text, so only the dense side of these 384 chunks is partial.\nToken-aware chunking is v1.3.2.\n\nrelease.yml: snapshot cache key r1 -> r2 (ingestion code changed, per\nthe key's own comment). HANDOFF.md: section 9 documents the audit.",
